<title>JAPAN: Weak yen slowing pace of Japan surplus drop--EPA.</title>
<headline>Weak yen slowing pace of Japan surplus drop--EPA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The weakening of the yen has started to cause Japan's current account surplus to shrink more slowly, Economic Planning Agency (EPA) Vice Minister Shinpei Nukaya told a news conference on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;When we look at the mid- and long-term effects of the yen's weakness on the current account surplus, it has started to affect the pace at which it has been shrinking,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>In terms of volumes, growth in imports has become moderate, while exports are almost levelling off, he added.</p>
</text>
